            <div xml:id="d788">

                <pb facs="1067" n="947" xml:id="pg947"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/1267: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-27T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>31. Have just seen Yen. He tells me he telegraphed last night to Chinese
                    delegation the instructions described in my number 28, January 26th, 12 midnight
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">noon?</hi>].</p>
                <p>Shantung settlement seems therefore assured. I sincerely congratulate President,
                    Secretary and other members delegation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
